course: dictionary
lesson: 11143
title: Wiggly: bends and wriggles
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the words around them tell you which one the writer means. Wiggly is one of those words. Look at the clues in the sentence.
explain: «A relaxed, friendly dog has a loose, wiggly body, a soft open mouth and a tail that wags in wide, easy sweeps.» Here wiggly means moving with small, quick twisting movements. The clues are loose, relaxed and friendly, so it is about how the body moves.
explain: In art and maths, wiggly means something else: a line with many small curves or bends, not a straight line. Try your meaning in the sentence. If it still makes sense, you have found the right meaning.
fact: Wiggly means with many small curves or bends, not straight.
fact: Wiggly also means moving with small, quick twisting movements.
fact: A wiggly tooth is a loose tooth that may soon come out.
fact: Wiggly is an adjective, so it describes a thing, such as a wiggly worm.
fact: Its forms are wiggly, wigglier and wiggliest.
exercise: Sam draws a wiggly line in art. What does wiggly mean here? | *With many small curves or bends, not straight | Straight and neat | Very loud | Hot to touch
exercise: «A loose, wiggly body and a soft, open mouth usually mean a relaxed, friendly dog.» What does wiggly mean here? | *Moving with small, quick twisting movements | Made of wool | Straight and still | Very hungry
exercise: Which word is the comparative form of wiggly, for a line that bends even more? | wiggle | wiggly | *wigglier | wiggliest
test: Ella says, «My tooth is wiggly.» What does she mean? | *Her tooth is loose | Her tooth is bigger than her friends' teeth | Her tooth has many bends | Her tooth is shiny
test: «A stiff, high wag with a stiff body can mean danger, while a relaxed dog wags its whole wiggly body.» What does the context suggest about the wiggly body of the relaxed dog? | It is very cold | It is hidden under a blanket | It is stiff and still | *It moves in a loose, twisting way
exam: Which sentence uses wiggly to mean moving with small, quick twisting movements? | The road was wiggly and bent. | The wiggly sum was very easy. | A wiggly tooth is a bigger tooth. | *The tadpoles were wiggly, twisting quickly in the pond.
